RE: Christensen Road Modifications, Revision 2
Dear Mr. Cobb,
BenchMark Engineers, PC (BME) is pleased to provide your office with this scope of work and fee estimate
for various modifications to Christensen Road between Pershing Boulevard and US 30 in eastern
Cheyenne. In general, the work is anticipated to include addressing stormwater conveyance, site grading
that will allow for the future installation of power underground, three new drainage easements, one utility
easement, minor modifications to street lighting at Pershing, and platting the roadway right of way per
Laramie County standards. The following further details the anticipated scope of services:
SCOPE OF WORK
Easements
BME will work with Steil Surveying Services to define one (I) easement to place a High West Energy
power line to be placed underground along the western edge of the roadway in property owned by WJE,
LLC. Our team will also create up to three (3) easements to address the existing encroachment of a
culvert at properties owned by Kenrich, LLC, Capital Land and Home Co, LLC, and C and A Good
Holdings, LLC.
Drainage Improvements
To address the existing drainage issues in both the east and west ditches from the crest of Christensen,
south toward the intersection at Pershing, we will verify capacity in the existing storm sewer system and
review appropriate documents. We will utilize as-built drawings, as-built CAD files, as well as the final
drainage report completed by others for the constructed improvements, as provided by the city, to
complete our analysis and assist with our designs. We anticipate minimal additional site surveying, but we
will have the gas line at US 30 potholed for verification. Designs plans are anticipated to include grading
plans, storm sewer network extensions on both sides of the roadway, and associated site improvements.
It is assumed the non-paved areas within the improvements will be seeded with dryland seed, rather than
irrigated sod. It is also assumed no trees will be incorporated within this project.
