### Page 10 of 11

```text
Intersection Lighting
BME will use city-standard drawings and details for the replacement of the streetlights at Pershing
Boulevard. Our plans will not include any electrical or structural designs. Additionally, our scope of
services does not include any designs associated with lighting the intersection at US 30 or coordination
with WYDOT for lighting the intersection.
Signage Upgrades
BME will provide recommendations for signage improvements near the Pershing intersection. We have
included fees to provide solar-powered flashers on Pershing west of the intersection. Based on feedback
from city staff we will include the proposed recommendations into the final plans.
Submittals
We will provide designs submittals at the 65%, 95%, and final design plans for the city’s review and
approval. We will also provide an Engineer’s Cost estimate for the proposed improvements. BME will also
provide design plans to WYDOT and Laramie County for their concurrence. We will address comments
prior to bidding. We will prepare final estimated quantities, per city standards for use in bidding
documents.
Construction Administration
BME staff will attend a pre-bid meeting, provide responses for any addenda, and attend the bid opening.
During construction we will attend a pre-construction meeting and provide limited, part-time construction
observation and inspection services. We will review submittals, provide responses to requests for
information, and verify requests for payment. We will attend a walk-thru with the contractor and city
staff, and document items for a punch list of items to be corrected prior to acceptance. BME will prepare
as-build drawings based on the contractor’s redlines, city staff redlines, and our observations.
Coordination and Miscellaneous
BME will coordinate and communicate with city staff during the design and construction phases to
appropriately address the issues of the corridor. We will communicate with property owners regarding
the
respective
easements and
proposed
improvements
and
keep
the
city
informed
of these
communications. Although the limits of this project are not within the annexed area of the City of
Cheyenne, we will utilize the current edition of the City of Cheyenne and Board of Public Utilities Construction
Specifications and Standard Drawings as the standard specifications for this project and to develop bid items
and quantities, rather than the adopted standards of WYDOT or Laramie County.
Platting the Right of Way
BME will assist the city in platting the right-of-way for the Christensen Road corridor from north of the
Union Pacific Railroad to US 30 per Laramie County standards. Since this land is wholly within Laramie
County, it will go through the county’s process, rather than the city’s process. Previously, we had
recommended the roadway be platted following construction, which numerous city engineers agreed to.
For this, we will work with Steil Surveying Services to complete the process.
BenchMark Engineers
Christensen Road Improvements, R2
